    "datasource": "Kodak Pro 100 / PRN, Pro 100T / PRT, Pro 400 / PPF, Pro 400 MC / PMC and Pro 1000 / PMZ colour negative films, publication E-182, February 1997; SHA256 43f9be571f731356d868993dce6760c1f0254d04c50bf09b761027c5d0bd60cc. Reproduce with scripts/bw_expansion/prepare_colour_film.py; axis calibration derived from the page by scripts/bw_expansion/extract_graphs.py; source points, assumptions and conditions: data/profile-sources/kodak-pro-400mc-pmc/recipe.json. Dye spectra: fujifilm_pro_400h shapes, scaled so their mixture reproduces this sheet's own midscale-neutral-minus-D-min. PCHIP of the three plotted log-sensitivity traces; engine covers 380-780 nm, each trace is used only over its own plotted span and is unmeasured elsewhere. Relative shape only; the panel's E.N.D. density criterion is not an absolute speed. Measured, not assumed: the sheet's D-min trace is the spectral base density, and what the Status M densitometer reads through it is subtracted from the characteristic curves. Spectral adaptation parameters are not this stock's own: they are borrowed from fujifilm_pro_400h. The same stock whose dye shapes this sheet is prepared with. Density curves balanced against a rendered 5-stop grey ramp by scripts/bw_expansion/balance_against_ramp.py (upstream's correct_positive_curves_with_gray_ramp): density scale [0.9813, 1.0285, 0.9779], log-exposure shift [-0.2245, 0.0, -0.1517], data_trustability 0.5. Worst channel deviation from neutral across the ramp 26.2% before, 5.2% after. This correction is fitted against the engine, not measured from the datasheet. Density curves balanced against a rendered 5-stop grey ramp by scripts/bw_expansion/balance_against_ramp.py (upstream's correct_positive_curves_with_gray_ramp): density scale [0.9957, 0.9969, 0.9958], log-exposure shift [-0.0, 0.0, 0.0], data_trustability 0.5. Worst channel deviation from neutral across the ramp 5.2% before, 5.1% after. This correction is fitted against the engine, not measured from